response:
 Denote Plane $ABC~$ as $ax+by+cz=1$. Since it's distance from origin is $1$, we have $|a^2+b^2+c^2|=\frac{1}{1^2}=1$. We know the equation of the plane
\begin{align*}
\overrightarrow{OA}&=t\overrightarrow{n}=\frac{s}{a}\overrightarrow{i} \\
\overrightarrow{OB}&=u\overrightarrow{n}=\frac{s}{b}\overrightarrow{j} \\
\overrightarrow{OC}&=v\overrightarrow{n}=\frac{s}{c}\overrightarrow{k}
\end{align*}
Thus, $$p=\frac{s}{3a},q=\frac{s}{3b},r=\frac{s}{3c}$$
So $$\frac{1}{p^2}+\frac{1}{q^2}+\frac{1}{r^2}=\frac{9}{s^2}\left(a^2+b^2+c^2\right)=\frac{9}{s^2}\cdot 1=\boxed{9}$$. <answer> $9$ </answer>

